<p>Building off what <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anactualcrow" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6040770); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6040770&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608458115" alt="AnActualCrow" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6040770)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anactualcrow" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6040770); return false;">AnActualCrow</a></span> said, my concern with your central narrative section is that it doesn't really&#8230;do anything? There's this kinda, little mystery but there's not really a lot of time spent developing it and also bear in mind: this is a SCP article. Your addenda/discovery section exploring the mystery is going to come after the Description of what the SCP is, and so the reader will already know that the answer to the question 'where did the man get all the coins from' is 'infinite quarter'.</p>
<p>The idea of the Foundation using this for funding is interesting and building off that so it goes somewhere could be really fun: it might be worth considering like, how this could break something or draw unwanted attention that causes conflict.</p>

